# the die — a node that is nothing but the far end of an edge (card:edge.md, day one, 2026-09-02).
# It rolls once into its state and waits to be let go: pulled, it stays up; the last puller gone, it
# idles out.  Too simple as a program, Henri said, and exactly right as a fixture — there is nothing
# in it but the edge.  `pulse roll` is the roll's mtime, so idle counts from the roll, not from a log
allow die.py
no-net
pulse roll
idle 30
program /usr/bin/python3 $NODE/die.py --state $STATE
